messages:   18%|#8        | 90/500 [00:21<01:28,  4.65it/s] 18%|#8        | 91/500 [00:22<01:31,  4.49it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 91 and 93?', '<think>\nTo find the product of 91 and 93, I can use the difference of squares formula. \n\nFirst, I recognize that 91 is 92 minus 1 and 93 is 92 plus 1. \n\nUsing the formula (a - b)(a + b) = a² - b², I substitute a with 92 and b with 1. \n\nCalculating 92 squared gives me 8464, and subtracting 1 squared (which is 1) results in 8463. \n\nTherefore, the product of 91 and 93 is 8463.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **91** and **93**, we can use the **difference of squares** method for an efficient calculation.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n91 \\times 93 &= (92 - 1)(92 + 1) \\\\.\n&= 92^2 - 1^2 \\quad \\text{(Using the identity } (a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2) \\\\.\n&= 8464 - 1 \\\\.\n&= 8463.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\].\n\n**Final Answer:**.\n\n\\[.Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
