messages:   96%|#########6| 482/500 [01:52<00:03,  4.93it/s] 97%|#########6| 483/500 [01:52<00:03,  5.39it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 93 and 79?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 93 and 79, I can use the standard multiplication method.\n\nFirst, I'll break down 93 into 90 and 3, and 79 into 70 and 9.\n\nNext, I'll multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n- 90 multiplied by 70 equals 6,300.\n- 90 multiplied by 9 equals 810.\n- 3 multiplied by 70 equals 210.\n- 3 multiplied by 9 equals 27.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these products together to get the total sum, which is 7,337.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **93** and **79**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe'll use the standard multiplication method by breaking down the numbers into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n93 \\times 79 = (90 + 3) \\times (70 + 9)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n1. **Multiply 90 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 70 = 6,\\!300\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply 90 by 9:**\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 9 = 810\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply 3 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 70 = 210\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Multiply 3 by 9:**\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 9 = 27\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, add all the results from the previous step to get the final product.\n\n\\[\n6,\\!300 + 810 + 210 + 27 = 7,\\!337\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{7,\\!337}\n\\].Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
